{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/103281-interactions-between-angels-and-demons","id":103281,"title":"Interactions between Angels and Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-01T03:14:35-07:00","id":103281,"title":"Interactions between Angels and Demons","content":"I am still trying to wrap my head round the interaction between angels and demons from the RAW perspective.<br /> <br /> 1. Spoofing.<br /> <br /> It seems obvious that when an angel meets a demon, the demon can try to spoof it. This is implied by the write up of the Flagged condition and also in the How an Angel Dies story. But what exactly is being spoofed? As far as I can tell Angels don't have any overt means to identify demons as such. They do so, as far as I can tell, by implication - was the demon compromised and is now flagged or surveilled? Is the demon being followed by Aether-seeking stigamtics or cryptids? Is the demon doing something overtly supernatural like taking on a demonic form?<br /> <br /> Is that correct? I.e. if an angel is standing next to a demon who has not been compromised, who is acting perfectly in character and who is not doing anything suspicious then spoofing would not even come into play. What about if the angels is suspicious but the demon is still acting innocuously and has not provoked a compromise? That in itself will not trigger spoofing, right? The angel may well try to act on its suspicion and try to provoke a compromise but spoofing is irrelevant until that happens as far as I can see.<br /> <br /> One more thing on spoofing. It can't be used in demonic form. Does that include partial transformation?<br /> <br /> 2. Ongoing Cover deterioration<br /> <br /> Now suppose spoofing failed, you've been compromised and now you are standing next to an angel who *knows* that you are a demon. You failed your last compromise roll and lost a point of Cover. What happens next? The introduction story (p.15) talked about Cover &quot;fraying&quot; as a group of hunter angels advanced on Sonya until she knew that she could never keep that cover. That suggests to me that the demon would just keep throwing compromise rolls until its cover is gone. The description of The Brilliant angel on p.220 suggests something similar. But how does that play out under RAW? Is simply standing next to an angel who knows you are a demon causing to throw new compromise rolls? How often? Every turn?!<br /> <br /> And how does that interact with the idea of a Compromised Agency? It must be possible for a demon to be a collaborationist. But if a compromised agency is run by an angel who knows all the demons in it would just shred their cover. Or for an &quot;honest&quot; demon to regularly interact with an angel in order to convince it to Fall for example (e.g. Alexandra Fairchild, p. 219).<br /> <br /> I am assuming for this to make sense there must be some sort of &quot;action&quot; that an Angel can take in order to &quot;push against the Cover&quot; once it knows someone is a demon. Is it a Numina? Or just a part of angelic nature? How would it work? An instant action or an extended one? Does it consume Essence? Can it be activated remotely once the angel knows someone is a demon or do they have to be in their vicinity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T06:01:21-07:00","id":103327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/103281-interactions-between-angels-and-demons#post103281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am still trying to wrap my head round the interaction between angels and demons from the RAW perspective.<br /> <br /> 1. Spoofing.<br /> <br /> It seems obvious that when an angel meets a demon, the demon can try to spoof it. This is implied by the write up of the Flagged condition and also in the How an Angel Dies story. But what exactly is being spoofed? As far as I can tell Angels don't have any overt means to identify demons as such. They do so, as far as I can tell, by implication - was the demon compromised and is now flagged or surveilled? Is the demon being followed by Aether-seeking stigamtics or cryptids? Is the demon doing something overtly supernatural like taking on a demonic form?<br /> <br /> Is that correct? I.e. if an angel is standing next to a demon who has not been compromised, who is acting perfectly in character and who is not doing anything suspicious then spoofing would not even come into play. What about if the angels is suspicious but the demon is still acting innocuously and has not provoked a compromise? That in itself will not trigger spoofing, right? The angel may well try to act on its suspicion and try to provoke a compromise but spoofing is irrelevant until that happens as far as I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div> From the wording of the Blown Condition, I would suspect that Angels -do- have demon-detecting powers. &quot;You cannot spoof Angels, God-Machine cultists, or anyone with the Unseen Sense (God-Machine) merit.&quot; Its possibly an oversight when they were writing up angels in the Demon book. Indeed, for the most part, angels are detailed in the God Machine Chronicle rules update, which unsurprisingly doesn't come with rules for sensing demons. DtD only includes a few numina which, by nature, are optional.<br /> <br /> What I do, instead, is assume that, like Stigmatics, Angels come with Unseen Sense (God-Machine). Spirits naturally can sense sources of essence that they can feed off of, can they not? Including recognizing werewolves? Ghosts can sense Sin Eaters and other ghosts. I think its the same thing. The chapter on Ephemeral Entities didn't quite cover it, but I think its a bit implied. Spirits recognize werewolves and wolf blooded, but we don't get mechanics for it. Ghosts have to recognize SEs, since being bothered by them is a big thing in that game. I think its the same thing here.<br /> <br /> So, if an angel is around and you don't spoof, it just knows you're a demon. I think that's how it works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One more thing on spoofing. It can't be used in demonic form. Does that include partial transformation? </div> </div> </div> I would think that it could, as one can hide a number of physical alterations under clothes. As well, actions while under partial transformations still call for Compromise checks, and you still use Cover as your supernatural resistance, so one's cover is at least partially still up.<br /> <br /> If a demon's being obvious of the partial transformation, however, I would call for more Compromise checks from witnesses, and prevent spoofing from working, since, well, obvious is obvious! <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Ongoing Cover deterioration<br /> <br /> Now suppose spoofing failed, you've been compromised and now you are standing next to an angel who *knows* that you are a demon. You failed your last compromise roll and lost a point of Cover. What happens next? The introduction story (p.15) talked about Cover &quot;fraying&quot; as a group of hunter angels advanced on Sonya until she knew that she could never keep that cover. That suggests to me that the demon would just keep throwing compromise rolls until its cover is gone. The description of The Brilliant angel on p.220 suggests something similar. But how does that play out under RAW? Is simply standing next to an angel who knows you are a demon causing to throw new compromise rolls? How often? Every turn?!<br /> <br /> And how does that interact with the idea of a Compromised Agency? It must be possible for a demon to be a collaborationist. But if a compromised agency is run by an angel who knows all the demons in it would just shred their cover. Or for an &quot;honest&quot; demon to regularly interact with an angel in order to convince it to Fall for example (e.g. Alexandra Fairchild, p. 219).<br /> <br /> I am assuming for this to make sense there must be some sort of &quot;action&quot; that an Angel can take in order to &quot;push against the Cover&quot; once it knows someone is a demon. Is it a Numina? Or just a part of angelic nature? How would it work? An instant action or an extended one? Does it consume Essence? Can it be activated remotely once the angel knows someone is a demon or do they have to be in their vicinity? </div> </div> </div> Well, I would consider that acting against an angel would count as grossly acting out of cover. After that, using certain embeds and exploits and partial transformations (the powerful ones you need to survive) would be calling for checks. Or acting grossly out of character again - Tommy the librarian would not be using a gun, or be fighting angels.<br /> <br /> Remember that its every action that's out of character. And remember that every roll suffers a penalty of equal to the angel's rank at least, potentially more depending on what condition the Unchained was inflicted with when it was revealed.<br /> <br /> So, in the case of our story demon, it went something like this. Turn 1) lose cover from healing, supernatural effect. Get a condition. Turn 2) Angels show up, spot demon, cause another compromise check. Likely upgrade condition. Turn 3) gets pissed and goes loud, destroying the cover completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":".  Fixed some formatting 04-01-2014, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}